>     Previous state was Needs-Build until 2004 Aug 23 11:38:18

> AIUI, his can be simply that noone has signed the (potentially) built
> package yet. On the other hand, I remember reading that packages can
> sometimes get stuck in this stage and require manual intervention from a
> buildd admin.=20

http://buildd.debian.org/build.php?&pkg=3Dcdtool&ver=3D2.1.5-10&arch=3Dalph=
a&file=3Dlog

This URL shows that no build logs have been uploaded for this package.
This means either the package is still in the process of being built,
it's been accepted by the buildd (goedel) for building but the build
hasn't actually started yet, or the package got lost somewhere along the
way.

According to the stats page, however, cdtool was in Needs-Build until
2004 Sep 05 17:01:21; this looks to me like a buildd admin has already
noticed the problem and reset the package, giving it another shot at
building.

If this were not the case, you would have wanted to contact
alpha@buildd.debian.org about this problem.

Cheers,
--=20
